Ladybird’s WebDriver clear algorithm now leaves a textarea rendering
the same empty value that its value IDL attribute reports. The
other engines’ drivers clear a textarea by setting its value from
script, so their rendering follows the value setter: geckodriver’s
clearResettableElement() in interaction.sys.mjs sets el.value to
the empty string, and the FormElementClear.js automation atom that
safaridriver uses in WebKit does the same.
